    "detail": "First published 1901 in 'New Jubilee Songs as Sung by the Fisk Jubilee Singers', collected by John W. Work II and Frederick J. Work, Nashville; the spiritual itself was in oral circulation long before that printing.",
    "sourceEdition": "Work, J. W. II and F. J. Work, 'New Jubilee Songs as Sung by the Fisk Jubilee Singers', Nashville, 1901",
    "notes": "Melody and changes only; no lyrics. The traditional spiritual is encoded, not any later arranged or recorded treatment. Notated in 4/4; gospel performance often leans the eighths toward a 12/8 shuffle, which is carried by feel=swing rather than by the meter. The tune is minor-pentatonic (1 b3 4 5 b7) over a modal i-iv vamp with a V7 turnaround, so deg 7 is the natural b7 by design, not a missing leading tone."
